## Summary

Security tests and one fix (Bead blog-hh6c).

- **Regression tests:** `packages/web/src/lib/safe-url.test.ts` now commits the bypass shapes from the blog-wmyj security review. Each case is checked against the document link and credit rule:
  - percent-encoded schemes;
  - control characters in or before the scheme;
  - backslash forms;
  - credentials;
  - protocol-relative and relative forms;
  - million-character values;
  - non-string inputs.
- **Fix:** the Codex review found that `mailto://user:secret@host/` kept its credentials through both `safeHref` and the document URL rule. WHATWG URLs parse userinfo in `mailto://` too. Only web addresses may carry credentials, so both rules now reject a `mailto:` address with a user name or password. Plain `mailto:reader@host`, query parameters, several recipients and percent-encoded addresses stay valid. Every caller inherits the rule: reader blocks, media credits, portability and owner contracts.

## Verification (host)

- `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm lint`, `pnpm format:check`, `test:quality-contract`: clean.
- `pnpm test:coverage`: all tests passed, including 952 safe-URL cases.

## Review

Tests implemented by the Codex worker. The Codex review held them on the missing `mailto://` credentials case. The coordinator added the rejection to both rules (6e0216a), and a narrow Codex re-review passed it. That re-review probed 33 more URLs across three document contexts and confirmed every caller inherits the rule.
